KNOWNBUG
justice-fairness1.aag
--bound 5
^\[justice0\] : PROVED up to bound 5$
^\[fairness0\] : PROVED up to bound 5$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
AIGER justice sets describe fair-loop witness conditions, while
fairness constraints restrict which witness loops are considered.  They
are not ordinary universal LTL properties.  EBMC currently lowers this
model's justice and fairness entries to standalone GF properties and
reports both as PROVED.  The justice polarity is therefore opposite to
the fair-loop witness interpretation, and the standalone fairness result
is fabricated.  This test remains a KNOWNBUG until AIGER justice and
fairness semantics are represented explicitly or the unsupported input is
rejected.
